        "question_type": "Objective",
        "exam_year": "2023",
        "question_text": "<p>For the reaction $N_2(g) + 3H_2(g) \\rightleftharpoons 2NH_3(g)$, what is the effect of increasing the pressure on the equilibrium position?</p>",
        "question_image": null,
        "answer_image": null,
        "explanation": "<p>According to Le Chatelier's Principle, increasing the pressure shifts the equilibrium to the side with fewer moles of gas. In this reaction, the left side has 4 moles of gas ($1 N_2 + 3 H_2$), and the right side has 2 moles of gas ($2 NH_3$). Thus, the equilibrium shifts to the right, favoring the formation of $NH_3$.</p>",
        "reference_passage": null,
        "novel": null,
        "comments_count": 0,
        "options": [
            {
                "option_id": "71486",
                "tag": "a",
                "text": "Shifts to the left",
